I say this game is better than people are giving it credit for, but I understand people's gripes with it. It is short as all hell (I beat this game in like 8h tops, side quests included, for the most part) and the story ends abruptly, setting up for an obvious sequel. And sure, that's kind of annoying, you should get a bit more bang for your buck, but I do believe it's a solid game, for what it is.
PROS:
-The gameplay and mechanics are solid (apart from the 3rd person mechanic which I thought was, overall, better handled in Human Revolution);
-The ambience and soundtrack are right there with HR, with the added element of gorgeous graphics and design, to boot;
-Super cool new Augs and really improved upon stealth.
CONS:
-The story is relatively interesting and you get quite a bit out of the side quests, but it won't blow your mind and it definitely feels unfinished and too short;
-The game doesn't run extremely well on PC, even if you actually take the graphics down to medium ( :'[ )
TL, DR: Great game but unfinished. Still haven't played through the DLC, but I'm guessing it's more of a side quest than added, relevant, content. I hope the inevitable sequel isn't a let down where the story is cocerned.

